course: dictionary
lesson: 10480
title: Muddy or unclear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe water and some describe thoughts. Turbid is one of them. When water is turbid, it is cloudy or muddy because mud, sand or other bits have been stirred up in it, so you cannot see clearly through it.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The turbid river was brown with mud after the storm.» Brown and mud are the clues, so turbid must mean cloudy or muddy. Test it: "The muddy river was brown with mud" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Turbid can also describe thoughts or writing that are confused and unclear. This use is formal, so you will meet it more in adult books than in everyday talk. Clear water lets light through, but turbid water lets less light through, which is why scientists test it.
fact: Turbid means cloudy or muddy, because bits are stirred up in the liquid.
fact: Turbid water lets less light through than clear water.
fact: Kipling calls the Amazon «the turbid Amazon», so the word describes real rivers too.
fact: The Amazon is in South America; it carries more water than any other river on Earth.
fact: In formal writing, turbid can describe confused or unclear thoughts.
exercise: «The turbid river was brown with mud after the storm.» What does turbid mean? | *Cloudy and muddy | Fast and noisy | Clear and sparkling | Very cold and icy
exercise: Water becomes turbid when what happens? | It is poured into a clean glass | *Mud, sand or other bits are stirred up in it | It is completely empty | It is frozen solid
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the river in «the turbid Amazon». | *turbid | river | the | Amazon
test: «The pond was turbid after the cows walked through it.» What made the water cloudy? | *Mud and bits were stirred up | Leaves had blown off the trees | The sun had dried it up | The water was frozen
test: A turbid argument is best described as what? | Loud and cheerful | *Confused and unclear | Clear and easy to follow | Happy and calm
exam: Which sentence uses turbid correctly? | *The turbid lake was brown with mud after the flood | The turbid lake was clear enough to see every fish | The turbid dog ran home happily | The turbid cake was sweet and golden
